{"name":"Orange Piñata","hex":"#ff6611","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"piñata","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A doll or other decorated container that is filled with candy and hit with a hammer or a stick by blindfolded children during birthday parties or other celebrations until the candy falls out.","Something which is repeatedly hit or damaged over a period of time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit something or someone with sticks after having filled them with candy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pi%C3%B1ata"}],"entries":[{"title":"Piñata","blocks":[{"text":"A piñata is a container, often made of papier-mâché, pottery, or cloth, that is decorated, filled with candy, and then broken as part of a celebration. Piñatas are commonly associated with Mexico."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/PI%C3%91ATA.jpg/330px-PI%C3%91ATA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pi%C3%B1ata","wikidata":"Q673051"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pi%C3%B1ata_Animation.gif/500px-Pi%C3%B1ata_Animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Pi%C3%B1ata_Animation.gif/500px-Pi%C3%B1ata_Animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman strikes a piñata at a celebration.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APi%C3%B1ata_Animation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/MonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG/500px-MonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/MonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG/1280px-MonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/MonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG/500px-MonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Franciscan friar hitting a piñata in Acolman, Mexico State","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonkPi%C3%B1ataAcolman1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Traditional_Mexican_Pi%C3%B1atas_02.jpg/500px-Traditional_Mexican_Pi%C3%B1atas_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Traditional_Mexican_Pi%C3%B1atas_02.jpg/1280px-Traditional_Mexican_Pi%C3%B1atas_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","